    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4192" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">astu</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">asty</span></b> , <i><span class="en">Vitr. 8, 3</span></i>;
			<i><span class="en">7</span></i> praef.),
		n., indecl., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄστυ</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a city</i>, esp. <i>Athens</i> (as urbs <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατ̓
				ἐξοχήν</span> for Rome): omnes qui arcem astuque accolunt
			cives, Att. ap. <i><span class="en">Non. p. 4, 330</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">An in astu venit?</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ter.
					Eun. 5, 5, 17</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">demigrare ex agris et in astu,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Leg. 2, 2, 5</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Nep.
				Them. 4, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Alcib. 6, 4</span></i>.</div>
